data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":606,"item_id":"msg_023585a31f9d93fc016b0311fa559487d1b91cfd3c9be8eb13","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"reviews\":[{\"actor\":\"ash-1\",\"decision\":\"reuse\",\"ability\":\"bark-extraction\",\"reason\":\"The implemented capability already assesses actual material and separates a finite branch outer layer with a personally inspected stone or flint contact. It does not infer harvestable trunk tissue from a tree label or create bark from branch stock. The observed tree represents branch stock, not a standing bark reserve; that distinction must remain intact. Your owned stones may satisfy the tool requirement after the required inspection. Neither assessment nor the available branch quantity guarantees a full bark unit.\",\"specification\":\"Reuse the existing bark-extraction contract and public schema unchanged, including its shared actor, target, tool and process references. Individual learning takes two rounds; review supplies neither mastery nor materials. Assessment costs one round and 0.2 energy and reports only represented, reachable material. Peeling requires eligible owned material and an inspected reusable stone/flint contact, with two active work-round equivalents and two energy per original branch unit, reduced proportionally for fractional or previously peeled inputs. Unrepresented standing tissue remains ineligible. For unspecified intact branches, partition at most 10% of existing mass into outer bark; preserve the remaining core, round usable bark quantities down to exact tenths, and retain residual mass as bark-fines. Preserve provenance and actual partial progress. Use actual interaction reach and shared collision geometry. Apply the registered progress, completion and cancellation contract; death cancels active work without duplicating or deleting escrow or losing remaining-work accounting. This is functional reuse, not a new implementation or permission to collect stock remotely.\",\"experienceReview\":\"Assessment can support grounded-understanding only when an actual test confirms qualified new information through information-confirmed: personal amount 0.8, cap 1, duration 8 rounds, refresh repetition with a 12-round cooldown; maintained gain 0.035 and decay 0.0015 under the existing rule. Completed paid peeling can qualify for the existing practice:bark-extraction source through practice-confirmed only at its registered real-output milestones: amount 0.4, cap 0.5, duration 8 rounds, refresh with a 12-round cooldown; maintained gain 0.02 and decay 0.001. These are bounded personal feedback, not rewards for requesting, learning, labels, mastery or every repeated operation. Do not add alias sources. Peeling itself supplies no direct nutrition, healing, thermal comfort or survival benefit.\",\"visualReview\":\"Use the existing declared events bark-assessed, bark-peeling-started, bark-peeling-progress, bark-peeling-completed and bark-peeling-stopped. Bind assessment text to observed eligibility and uncertainty, and progress/replay to paid work, actual remaining work, separated bark or fines and the changed core. Display only outputs actually produced; do not depict trunk stripping, a completed bark unit or a drying tray before those states exist. Information-confirmed and practice-confirmed subscriptions retain their existing qualification checks.\",\"learning\":2}]}","logprobs":[]}

